From d66b98dfca795112b43323f654f7f075b2980765 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wmehanna <wassimmehanna@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:54:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(vmapple): add vmapple-virtio-usb-pci device port
 (106b:1a01)

Model the virtio function behind macOS's AppleVirtIOUSBDeviceController,
written from the guest driver's observed behaviour in the 26B131 kernel
collection: queue 0 carries host requests (le32 length, endpoint, type,
payload) into 128 KiB guest buffers, queue 1 carries the guest's
responses (type, endpoint, data). Both streams go to a chardev with a
small length-prefixed framing, so a userspace USB host can enumerate
the guest as a USB device and run usbmux over its bulk pipes.
---
